---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/site.config';
import profPic from '@/assets/images/profile.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout title={SITE.name}>
  <article class="prose prose-sm sm:prose-base max-w-2xl">
    <div class="not-prose mb-8 flex items-center gap-5 sm:gap-6">
      <img
        src={profPic.src}
        alt={`Photo of ${SITE.name}`}
        width="128"
        height="128"
        class="border-line size-20 shrink-0 rounded-full border object-cover sm:size-28"
      />
      <h1 class="font-display text-ink text-3xl font-medium sm:text-4xl">{SITE.name}</h1>
    </div>

    <p>
      Data scientist focused on bringing data science to public policy, driven by the belief that
      better data and better analysis lead to better decisions. As co-lead of the data science team
      at CPC Analytics, I work with clients at the World Health Organization and international NGOs
      to put this into practice. I help decision-makers act on sound evidence, whether by tracking
      an outbreak as it unfolds, tracing how development finance is allocated, or synthesizing the
      latest research on the questions they face.
    </p>

    <p>
      I work across the full data pipeline, primarily in Python and R, from conception to finished
      product. My work has appeared in{' '}
      <em>The Lancet Global Health</em> and <em>Emerging Infectious Diseases</em>.
    </p>

    <p>
      I'm originally from the San Francisco Bay Area and now based in Berlin. Outside of work, I
      enjoy playing volleyball with my local club. Passing the German C1 exam in 2026 was a
      milestone I'm particularly proud of.
    </p>

    <p>
      Have a look at what I've worked on <a href="/work">here</a>, or send me a message at{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
